// The whole run, start to finish: set up, drive the session
// (go/a/session/phase/), tear down (go/a/teardown/). Every stage after
// setup() runs unconditionally -- a socket that never connected makes every
// send/recv into it fail fast and harmlessly (idstd's sys/io/ipc/sock/README.md),
// the same way qmon.py's background reader thread had nothing to read -- so
// there is no separate "did setup succeed" branch to thread through here.
// Not cased: run() calls setup() (setup/boot.id), which pairs a real,
// freshly-spawned qemu process against sockets no given can see in advance
// and races connecting to them -- see setup/boot.id's own note. A void
// function could still take a weak, outcome-blind case here, but drive()
// below cannot, and splitting cases between the two functions of one call
// chain for that reason would be worse than skipping both.
run() {
  setup();
  phase_wait();
} return void;

// Not cased: drive()'s return is (import qm_rc), set deep inside the same
// setup() race (setup/boot.id's note) -- so the one value a case here must
// match exactly is not decided by drive()'s own logic, only by which way
// that race happened to fall on the machine running the build.
drive() {
  run();
  cleanup();
  int rc = (import qm_rc);
} return int rc;
